{"id": "EUVD-2026-32452", "enisaUuid": "5f8e412b-7c11-3eff-9074-bbddf8ebe956", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmd/raid5: validate payload size before accessing journal metadata\n\nr5c_recovery_analyze_meta_block() and\nr5l_recovery_verify_data_checksum_for_mb() iterate over payloads in a\njournal metadata block using on-disk payload size fields without\nvalidating them against the remaining space in the metadata block.\n\nA corrupted journal contains payload sizes extending beyond the PAGE_SIZE\nboundary can cause out-of-bounds reads when accessing payload fields or\ncomputing offsets.\n\nAdd bounds validation for each payload type to ensure the full payload\nfits within meta_size before processing.", "datePublished": "2026-05-27T12:57:54", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T19:26:42", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c96c6f01d84b5c67db1bf1cc8591c0b7146826fc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ef4851d8324fd978ca1ff9ec76a275438f887743", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/28d3ff7109c66e99dc1b7cddacb5c760849620ef", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/33698bd1b2db9764a29df7751533d33967ff5c98", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c3a1cf78bd1bbb51b2cc5189b4743056553c1e0e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/73ce72edd113374801045924d4417199963f73a3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/406aa86394ead347c47428fb51b6359bdaa2257d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b0cc3ae97e893bf54bbce447f4e9fd2e0b88bff9"], "aliases": ["GHSA-76hh-2v3c-vm3v", "CVE-2026-46070"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "03e444d9-e134-3f1e-bbd2-0627fa270869", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.209"}, {"id": "134d1eae-59c4-3a86-8b66-f6bed5121789", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.27"}, {"id": "14f84ac8-b2df-3